Verification and Testing
Security Verification Checklist
Create a verification script to test all security measures:

nano ~/security_test.sh
Add the following content:

#!/bin/bash

echo "=== Prometheus Security Verification ==="
echo

# Test 1: HTTPS Configuration
echo "1. Testing HTTPS Configuration..."
if curl -k -s https://localhost:9090/metrics > /dev/null; then
    echo "   ✓ HTTPS is working on port 9090"
else
    echo "   ✗ HTTPS failed on port 9090"
fi

# Test 2: Authentication Required
echo "2. Testing Authentication Requirements..."
if curl -k -s https://localhost/ | grep -q "401\|Authentication"; then
    echo "   ✓ Authentication is required"
else
    echo "   ✗ Authentication not enforced"
fi

# Test 3: Admin Access
echo "3. Testing Admin Access..."
if curl -k -s -u admin:AdminPass123! https://localhost/api/v1/status/config | grep -q "global"; then
    echo "   ✓ Admin can access configuration"
else
    echo "   ✗ Admin access failed"
fi

# Test 4: Viewer Access
echo "4. Testing Viewer Access..."
if curl -k -s -u viewer:ViewerPass456! "https://localhost/api/v1/query?query=up" | grep -q "success"; then
    echo "   ✓ Viewer can query metrics"
else
    echo "   ✗ Viewer access failed"
fi

# Test 5: HTTP to HTTPS Redirect
echo "5. Testing HTTP to HTTPS Redirect..."
if curl -s -I http://localhost/ | grep -q "301\|302"; then
    echo "   ✓ HTTP redirects to HTTPS"
else
    echo "   ✗ HTTP redirect not working"
fi

# Test 6: SSL Certificate
echo "6. Testing SSL Certificate..."
if openssl s_client -connect localhost:443 -servername localhost < /dev/null 2>/dev/null | grep -q "Verify return code: 18"; then
    echo "   ✓ SSL certificate is present (self-signed)"
else
    echo "   ✗ SSL certificate verification failed"
fi

echo
echo "=== Security Test Complete ==="
Make the script executable and run it:

chmod +x ~/security_test.sh
./security_test.sh
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Certificate Errors
If you encounter certificate-related errors:

# Check certificate validity
openssl x509 -in /etc/ssl/prometheus/prometheus.crt -text -noout

# Verify certificate and key match
openssl x509 -noout -modulus -in /etc/ssl/prometheus/prometheus.crt | openssl md5
openssl rsa -noout -modulus -in /etc/ssl/prometheus/prometheus.key | openssl md5
Issue 2: Authentication Not Working
If authentication fails:

# Check htpasswd file format
sudo cat /etc/nginx/.htpasswd

# Test password manually
sudo htpasswd -v /etc/nginx/.htpasswd admin

# Check Nginx error logs
sudo tail -f /var/log/nginx/error.log
Issue 3: Service Connection Issues
If services cannot connect:

# Check port availability
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep -E "(9090|443|80)"

# Check firewall status
sudo ufw status

# Test internal connections
curl -k https://127.0.0.1:9090/metrics
Issue 4: Nginx Configuration Errors
If Nginx fails to start:

# Test configuration syntax
sudo nginx -t

# Check Nginx logs
sudo journalctl -u nginx -f

# Verify file permissions
ls -la /etc/ssl/prometheus/
